# Cursor Rules — Berkah POS KVM2

- Read root `AGENTS.md`, then follow its mandatory read order without skipping documents.
- Runtime source of truth: `AGENTS.md` and `docs/permanent/DOC_14_KVM2_ISOLATED_TENANT_ARCHITECTURE.md`.
- Logical config source of truth: `docs/permanent/DOC_00_CANONICAL_ARCHITECTURE_DECISION.md`.
- Runtime: Laravel 11 / PHP 8.3 / Filament 3 / Sanctum / stancl/tenancy v3 / MariaDB 11; one central DB and physically isolated database per tenant on the same private DB server.
- Active client code must not use Supabase SDK/Auth/RPC/Edge Functions, Supabase-hosted runtime config, RLS, or old Supabase sync tooling.
- Canonical config precedence is `GLOBAL -> TEMPLATE -> TENANT -> SERVICE -> DEVICE`.
- Canonical workbook: `config/FINAL_Production_Excel_A_WebC_Template_100Tenants.xlsx`.
- Run `python3 scripts/export_workbook_for_laravel.py --validate-only`; it must validate all 352 keys and the canonical hash before import.
- Do not merge POS and Akuntansi service rows.
- Central config tables are `global_configs`, `templates`, and `tenant_configs`; device overrides are in a tenant database's `device_configs`.
- Runtime cloud config uses the authenticated Laravel Central API, never direct mobile reads of configuration backing tables.
- Keep SQLite checkout writes and the local outbox atomic; do not claim cloud sync works until Laravel sync acceptance, acknowledgement, retry and conflict behavior are implemented and tested.
- Keep `btp-admin/` as a retired legacy/static notice only. New Admin is Filament at `/central/admin`, after a verified deployment.
- All changes through feature/fix/docs branches and reviewed PRs; no implementation commits directly to `main`.
- GitHub Actions use GitHub-hosted `ubuntu-24.04`.
- Do not claim staging/production readiness without executed evidence. Legacy hosted resources are deleted only after backup, reconciliation, cutover, retention review and explicit authorization.
